      "content": "hey, i need some help with how i'm phrasing things in public forums. lately the local news has been acting up with all this nonsense about the new municipal zoning changes and the transit strike, and i need to be able to discuss these things without looking like i'm paying too much attention to the \"surface\" stuff. i need to keep my profile low. how can i talk about these \"local distractions\" in a way that sounds totally mundane but acknowledges the underlying shifts without being obvious? i can't afford to look like i'm analyzing the theater.",
